"""Adroit pen re-orientation: verified replay of a library of open-loop finger plans.

Control law
-----------
The pen always starts in the same place and only the target axis changes from seed to seed, so
the joint-level motion that leaves the pen resting at a given orientation can be prepared in
advance. `LIBRARY` holds such motions ("plans"), found offline by a gradient-free search on a
copy of the plant (MAP-Elites over keyframes, one elite per 0.2 x 0.2 rad cell of the final
pen orientation; no learning, no network). A plan is three keyframes of the 24 servo set
points and the number of 10 ms steps spent moving to each: the set points are interpolated
linearly from the open hand through the keyframes, and the last keyframe is held to the end of
the episode. What each plan does to the pen is tabulated next to it (`LIB_*`).

At the first step of an episode the controller
  1. reads the target axis from the observation,
  2. ranks the plans whose tabulated final pen axis lies inside the success cone of the target
     (see `rank_plans`): robust and fast plans first, then the most central ones,
  3. rolls the best candidates out, one at a time, on its own copy of the plant (the model
     shipped with `hl_control`, used purely as a predictor) and scores each with the task's own
     condition (cos > 0.95 to the target and pen centre within 0.075 m of the reference on
     each of the last 25 steps). The first candidate that passes with the margins below is
     taken; if none passes, the best-scoring one is.
After that it replays the chosen plan, so the later calls are a table lookup. If the predictor
cannot be built, step 3 is skipped and the best-ranked plan is replayed as is.

Plant check (the only feedback). A replay is open loop, and a plan tuned on the nominal plant
often ends elsewhere when the pen is heavier or lighter, the surfaces more slippery or the
servos softer. The simulation is deterministic, so for the first `track_steps` steps the
controller also steps a predictor of each of those four documented variants with the actions
it applied and drops every variant whose prediction leaves the measured joints and pen state
by more than `match_tol`. If the nominal predictor is dropped and exactly one variant still
reproduces the measurements, the plant is that variant: the remaining steps are re-planned
with its predictor (keep the current plan if it still passes there, otherwise switch to the
plans whose tabulated outcome on that variant fits the target, verified from the steps already
executed). On the nominal plant, and whenever nothing matches exactly (noisy measurements,
an unknown plant), nothing changes and the nominal plan is replayed to the end.

Known limit: softer servos and a heavier or lighter pen show in the very first step, so the
switch is clean. Lower friction only shows when the pen lands (step 7-9); the plans switched in
that late rarely end where their table says, and the slippery plant stays the weak case. A
plant that is none of the documented ones gets the nominal plan and no correction at all.

Parameters (`PARAMS`)
---------------------
n_verify     : most candidates simulated at step 0 (each is one 2 s predictor rollout, ~50 ms).
cos_margin   : a candidate is accepted if its smallest cosine over the last 25 steps exceeds
               0.95 + cos_margin ...
dist_margin  : ... and the pen centre stays within 0.075 - dist_margin metres of the reference.
table_cone   : [deg] a plan is a candidate if angle(tabulated axis, target) + tabulated wander
               is below this (the success cone is 18.2 deg).
scen_cone    : [deg] a perturbed-plant outcome counts as "still good" inside this cone.
w_robust     : ranking weight per perturbed plant (weak, heavy, light) whose tabulated outcome of
               the plan is still good for this target. Small: those plants show at the first step,
               when switching plans is still free.
w_slip       : the same weight for the slippery plant. Large: lower friction only shows once the
               pen has landed (step 7-9), too late for a clean switch, so the plan chosen at step 0
               should already be one that ends at the target on the slippery plant as well.
w_fast       : ranking weight per step of tabulated settled time (earlier success, more return).
               Both weights are in degrees of centring: the rank also subtracts the table angle.
n_replan     : most library plans simulated when re-planning for an identified variant, taken
               from those whose tabulated outcome there has a cosine above replan_cos to the target.
track_steps  : how long the plant check runs (the pen lands on the hand around step 8; the
               variants separate from the nominal plant at the latest when it starts to slide).
match_tol    : largest deviation [rad, m, m/s, rad/s] between a predictor and the measurement
               that still counts as "the same plant" (exact arithmetic gives ~1e-12).
"""

